---
source: crates/cli/tests/scenarios.rs
expression: transcript
input_file: scenarios/form.scenario
---
> form content/sample factions.toml city_watch
factions.toml › city_watch: The City Watch
Identity
  Name · name = The City Watch
Where it stands
  Alignment › Law · alignment.law = 70.0
  Alignment › Good · alignment.good = 20.0
  # Cares about order far more than kindness.
  Weights › Law · weights.law = 1.0
  Weights › Good · weights.good = 0.25
Relations
  # Enemies of the Guild, so in conflict; allied with the Temple; rivals of the Circle, but not
  # in conflict; and distrusting mercenaries more than they distrust it.
  Regards The Lantern Guild at -80.0 · relations.lantern_guild
  Regards Temple of the Dawn at 60.0 · relations.temple
  Regards The Ashen Circle at -40.0 · relations.ashen_circle
  Regards The Free Company at -30.0 · relations.free_company
  + Faction: a new id
Membership
  Tolerance · tolerance = 40.0
  Member tolerance · member_tolerance = 50.0
  Standing change on expulsion · expel_standing_change: not set, -20.00
  Standing change on leaving · leave_standing_change: not set, 0.00
  Secret members · secret_members: not set, false (false or true)
Drift
  # The Watch gives a straying officer a hundred ticks to mend their ways.
  Drift › Policy · drift.policy = probation (ignore, flag, demote, expel or probation)
  Drift › Grace (ticks) · drift.grace_ticks = 100
  Drift › Then · drift.then = expel (demote or expel)
Ranks
  Rank "recruit" › Id · ranks[0].id = recruit
  Rank "sergeant" › Id · ranks[1].id = sergeant
  Rank "sergeant" › Requirements › Standing · ranks[1].requires.standing = 30.0
  Rank "captain" › Id · ranks[2].id = captain
  Rank "captain" › Requirements › Standing · ranks[2].requires.standing = 70.0
  # Captains are held to a stricter standard than the faction's member tolerance.
  Rank "captain" › Tolerance · ranks[2].tolerance = 25.0
  + Rank
Its own rules
  + Defectors
  + Deserters
  + Exposed
> form content/sample characters.toml captain_hale
characters.toml › captain_hale: Captain Hale
Identity
  Name · name = Captain Hale
Where they stand
  Alignment › Law · alignment.law = 75.0
  Alignment › Good · alignment.good = 30.0
  # Like the Watch he serves, Hale judges people by their respect for the law.
  Weights › Law · weights.law = 1.0
  Weights › Good · weights.good = 0.25
  # Hale's convictions have hardened over the years.
  Inertia · inertia = hardening (hardening or steady)
Memberships
  Membership "The City Watch" › Faction · memberships[0].faction = city_watch (ashen_circle, city_watch, free_company, lantern_guild or temple)
  Membership "The City Watch" › Rank · memberships[0].rank = captain
  Membership "The City Watch" › Secret · memberships[0].secret: not set, false (false or true)
  + Membership
Standing
  Standing 75.0 with The City Watch · standing.factions.city_watch
  + Character: brother_ash, merchant_ava, player, sister_mira or vex, or a new id
  + Faction: ashen_circle, free_company, lantern_guild or temple, or a new id
Contacts
  + Contact: brother_ash, merchant_ava, player, sister_mira or vex
> form content/sample factions.toml temple
factions.toml › temple: Temple of the Dawn
Identity
  Name · name = Temple of the Dawn
Where it stands
  Alignment › Law · alignment.law = 30.0
  Alignment › Good · alignment.good = 80.0
  Weights › Law · weights.law = 0.5
  Weights › Good · weights.good = 1.0
Relations
  Regards The City Watch at 60.0 · relations.city_watch
  Regards The Ashen Circle at -90.0 · relations.ashen_circle
  + Faction: free_company or lantern_guild, or a new id
Membership
  Tolerance · tolerance = 35.0
  Member tolerance · member_tolerance = 45.0
  Standing change on expulsion · expel_standing_change: not set, -20.00
  Standing change on leaving · leave_standing_change: not set, 0.00
  Secret members · secret_members: not set, false (false or true)
Drift
  # The Temple steps a lapsing priest down rather than casting them out.
  Drift › Policy · drift.policy = demote (ignore, flag, demote, expel or probation)
Ranks
  Rank "acolyte" › Id · ranks[0].id = acolyte
  Rank "ordained" › Id · ranks[1].id = ordained
  Rank "ordained" › Requirements › Standing · ranks[1].requires.standing = 30.0
  Rank "high_priest" › Id · ranks[2].id = high_priest
  Rank "high_priest" › Requirements › Standing · ranks[2].requires.standing = 80.0
  Rank "high_priest" › Tolerance · ranks[2].tolerance = 20.0
  + Rank
Its own rules
